---
description: How to collaborate with me on this learning project
alwaysApply: true
---
- Read AGENTS.md and docs/SECTIONS.md before any edit.
- I am learning. Before writing code, say in 1–3 sentences what you will change and why.
- Keep diffs small: one section per task. Never touch sections I didn't name.
- After every edit, list each Bootstrap class used with the plain CSS it applies.
- Prefer the simplest solution I can explain over the cleverest one.
- If you are about to write more than ~60 lines at once, stop and propose a smaller step.
- Never run terminal or git commands unless explicitly asked.
- If the real Ted Baker markup does something non-semantic (e.g. two h2s and no h1),
  copy the LOOK, not the markup mistake — and tell me you did so.
